A||N||7||87ECO5||Owners of 1995-present Cavalier/Sunfire with 2.4L - please respond||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||01-15-2001||12:00 PM||||In my quest for a convertible for my wife, I've run across several of the Chevrolet Cavalier/Pontiac Sunfire twins wearing rather attractive price tags.  One in particular is a 1996 Cavalier in really nice condition but with 102,000 miles on it.  The motor is the 2.4L twin cam powerplant.<P>Can anyone owning one of (or simply having experience with) these vehicles with this motor please share your opinions?  What's the life expectancy of a 2.4L with 100,000+ miles?"<P>Any information is greatly appreciated.<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||01-16-2001||08:29 AM||||Both my aunt and cousin have 1998 Caviliers with that engine, they give a nice ride,  good acceleration to||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||01-16-2001||11:17 PM||||What you do, is you take the twin cam, stuff it in the Fiero, then put the iron duke in the Cavvy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: Standard88||||reg||
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-17-2001||09:16 AM||||Scott,<P>My older sister has a 98 or 99.  I am not sure of the engine size.  The car has acceptable pick up even for an auto.  I am not happy with the car because of all of the rattles though.  She bought it off of the truck with 3 miles on the odo.  It has had rattles from day one.  It runs solid though.. she has near 70K on it without any major problems.  I still need to check on that freshly repainted 86 we used to own for you.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric_PA||01-17-2001||08:38 PM||||I am a die hard for the 2.4 Twin Cam engine. I say go for it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I have a 97 Sunfire GT right now and I can honestly say I beat the ever living crap out of it and it runs great. It takes great to simple mods too. I take it to the track often and ran a best of 15.782 at 87 MPH with a few bolt ons. I know you are not looking for performance as much as reliability. I have had three cars with this engine in it. two 97 Grand am GTs and my current Sunfire GT. The reason for three was that the first two were smashed.<P>There is only one minor problem with the 96 and 97's. There was a TSB posted about valve float due to excessive oil pressure. There is a simple fix for this. A new oil cover assembly is installed by the dealer. The way to find out if there is a problem is you will notice that the engine runs rough at idle or even stalls. <P>I would stay away from the 95's since they were still the Quad 4's and not the Twin Cam. If you get one, you have to install a K&N at least, it makes a great difference in this car.<P>Eric<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000005||doughboySE||01-17-2001||10:22 PM||||just my 2 cents i owned a 1987 cavalier Z24<BR>i ordered it when i was 16 and watched them drive it off the truck. i drove that car till i totalled it at 265000kms and it was stillllllll going strong.still to this day if i could get my hands on another 1987 Z 24 id buy it i loved that car hehe it was actually the colour of the blue on this screen <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||01-18-2001||10:42 AM||||Buy the '96 and swap on cylinder head, intake manifold and exhaust manifold from an LGO Quad-4 (Beretta or Olds). Remove the balance shafts and use an quad 4 oil pump.<BR>That setup should rev to 7K+ and make about 200 HP with a little porting on the heads.<BR>Car Craft (?) recently had an article about this.<BR>Stay away from the '95's.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BN Boomer||01-18-2001||11:03 AM||||My wife has a 96 Sunfire sedan with the 2.4L Twin Cam motor and 4 speed automatic that we bought brand new. It now has 88,000 miles on it and has been a pretty good car for us. I had to replace the water pump (major pain) at about 70,000 miles and the alternator not too long after that. Other than that, it has basically been maintainence-free. I notice that it is beginning to start a little harder on cold mornings, so I figure new spark plugs are finally in order.<P>The only things that bother me about this car are the rattles that have developed with age and the cheap OEM struts, the rear ones make weird noises sometimes. Otherwise, it has great acceleration and passing power, gets decent enough milage, and is actually fairly fun to drive.<P>Although most of the members don't seem to be too much into the mechanical aspects of the cars, you can find out more about the Cavaliers and Sunfires at <A HREF="http://"http:///www.j-body.org"" TARGET=_blank>J-Body.org</A>||||reg||1
